    "labelChirho": "Sihon (personal name)",
    "descriptionChirho": "Proper masculine name referring to Sihon, the Amorite king of Heshbon who refused Israel passage through his territory and was defeated in battle, with his land allocated to Reuben and Gad (Num 21:21-35, Deut 1:4, 2:24-36, 3:2-6, Josh 2:10, 9:10, 12:2,5, 13:10,21,27; Judg 11:19-21; Neh 9:22; Ps 135:11, 136:19). Transliterated uniformly: eng 'Sihon/Sichon', spa 'Sijón/Sihón', arb 'سيحون', kor '시혼', swa 'Sihoni', hin 'सीहोन'. The two clusters differ only by the prepositional lamed prefix, not by referent.",
    "senseIdsChirho": [120756, 120758]
  }
]
